# Security-critical ownership map for Project-mAIstro.
#
# This file names the accountable human authority for each surface below. It
# does NOT, by itself, enforce anything: GitHub only enforces code-owner review
# when the live ruleset sets `require_code_owner_review`, and the recorded
# read-back in `.github/live-merge-boundary.json` shows that flag is `false`
# on both the `develop` and `main` rulesets, as is `require_last_push_approval`,
# while `develop` requires zero approving reviews. See "Residual risk: no
# reviewer separation is enforced (#85)" in docs/ci/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md.
#
# Consequence, stated plainly: a PR touching any path below can be authored and
# merged by the same account while satisfying GitHub completely. Turning that
# separation on is a live-settings change owned by #564/#85 and must not be
# applied blindly — it can deadlock the autonomous queue, which relies on
# `develop`'s zero-approval posture and the admin bypass. Until then, treat these
# entries as review routing, not as a merge gate.

